meta {
  name: scan-table-second-restaurant
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/public/v1/t/{{qr_token_coastal}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

tests {
  test("responds 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
  })

  test("returns the OTHER restaurant", function () {
    // Tenant scoping: the same endpoint, a different token, and none of the first restaurant's
    // data (docs/DECISIONS.md D3).
    expect(res.body.data.menu.restaurant.slug).to.equal("coastal-curry")
  })

  test("its own rates apply", function () {
    // Coastal Curry charges a 10% service charge; Spice Garden charges none.
    expect(res.body.data.menu.service_charge_bps).to.equal(1000)
  })
}

docs {
  # Scan the second restaurant

Same endpoint, different token. Proves the multi-tenant path: a different menu, and a service charge
the first restaurant does not have.

Deliberately does **not** overwrite `guest_token` -- the rest of the collection runs against
Spice Garden.
}
